From: thefutureisprivate <contact@thefutureisprivate.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: try per-device board files

The FRITZ!Box 5690 Pro has two QCN9274 radios with separate factory
calibration records. A shared board.bin cannot hold both patched board
files. Try a bus- and device-specific name before the API 1 fallback,
keeping board-2.bin lookup and existing fallback behavior unchanged.

This follows the per-device calibration filename convention already used
by ath12k. Hardware validation on this board is still pending.

Signed-off-by: thefutureisprivate <contact@thefutureisprivate.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -521,7 +521,7 @@ int ath12k_core_fetch_board_data_api_1(s
 int ath12k_core_fetch_bdf(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct ath12k_board_data *bd)
 {
 	char boardname[BOARD_NAME_SIZE], fallback_boardname[BOARD_NAME_SIZE];
-	char *filename, filepath[100];
+	char *filename, filepath[100], per_device[64];
 	int bd_api;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -556,6 +556,13 @@ int ath12k_core_fetch_bdf(struct ath12k_
 		goto success;
 
 	bd_api = 1;
+	/* Some boards keep a separate, factory-patched BDF for each radio. */
+	snprintf(per_device, sizeof(per_device), "board-%s-%s.bin",
+		 ath12k_bus_str(ab->hif.bus), dev_name(ab->dev));
+	ret = ath12k_core_fetch_board_data_api_1(ab, bd, per_device);
+	if (!ret)
+		goto success;
+
 	ret = ath12k_core_fetch_board_data_api_1(ab, bd, ATH12K_DEFAULT_BOARD_FILE);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, filename,
